Fix handleClick: if action === 'modal-backdrop' only handle if event.target === actionEl, and don't preventDefault when target is inside modal (event.target !== actionEl). Better generic: actionEl = closest('[data-action]'); if actionEl is modal-backdrop and target !== actionEl, return (don't preventDefault). Also if button is submit, closest data-action may be backdrop, returning. So special-case.

Also modal action data-action nested might be on icon? svg inside button, closest yields button. fine.

